  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $(0,5]$\n\nII. $[1,3]$\n\nIII. $[-4,2]\\cup [6,9]$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[1,3]$ and $[-4,2]\\cup [6,9]$ are closed because:\n\n- The boundary points of $[1,3]$ are $1$ and $3.$ Both of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of $[-4,2]\\cup [6,9]$ are $-4,2,6,$ and $9.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not closed because $(0,5]$ has a boundary point $0,$ which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
